facts 58.3% of 163 -> FAIL (50/120 readings failed, 230 facts). On the 70 successful readings alone, moves taken from the world: first residences 52/55 = 94.5%, role facts 95/95; the archived 64/67 (95.5%, PASS) held 12 moves counted as first residences. The 3 misses (debug worlds, seed 11): each time the first residence and a move are in the same session ("X resides in A. X moved to B.") and the translator wrote only the current city; no city was invented and the later residence questions of these people were right or unknown, never asserted wrong | The deviation of n°89 is larger than disclosed: correctly computed, its gate fails twice, by the outage and, on the successful readings, by 94.5% < 95% once moves are classified from the world. The decision to spend would not have been taken; the measurement of n°89 itself is not affected (never-used worlds, its own criteria, no failed call) and stands. A first residence superseded by a move in the same session is now reported (superseded_in_session) and used by no existing gate; a future gate on first residences should leave them out, written before it is used. Cost check of the phase C' session: the tools priced it $0.263 (step 1, 70 calls) + $1.480 (step 2, 678 calls, Batch API) = $1.743; Khaled read 1.93 EUR for it on the Console: not reconciled yet (currency and VAT of the display unknown here; the Console's cost page by model and by batch would settle it). Tag v7.7.3 |
 
