y, reported); free_nonames (free questions read with the ontology's conventions but without the names in memory); free_template (free questions through the template: the dumb control); the always-unknown floor. Step 1, gate on debug worlds (seed 11, worlds 11000-11004, synchronous with the retries of n°90): G1, Khaled reads 30 pairs (canonical, free) drawn with a fixed seed among the reworded questions and finds at most 1 that does not ask the same thing; G2, free_names is at least 95% right with 0 asserted error, every question counted and a failed call counted as wrong (rule of n°90); G3, the validity check V holds on the debug set. If the gate fails: no measurement, the session stops, diagnosis on the debug worlds (everything is saved for them). Step 2, the measurement on never-used worlds: world v2, --seed 19 (worlds 19000-19009), 10 worlds x 12 sessions x 3 questions, Batch API with resume | V (validity of the set, read before any criterion): the template gives the canonical goal for at most 50% of the free questions, fallbacks included; if V fails the set does not test free questions and nothing is claimed. D1: free_names is at least 95% right with 0 asserted error. D3: free_names is at most 3 points below canon on the same questions, with no more asserted errors. A question whose reading call failed counts as wrong; a failed fact reading counts as an empty reading; both are reported. Claim if V, D1 and D3 pass, within this scope: synthetic worlds whose facts are paraphrased by the seeded generator and read with the shared lexicon; yes/no questions reworded by another model of the same family as the reader, with the polarity of the original; such questions are answered as well as canonical ones, without an asserted error. D2, a secondary hypothesis with its own pre-registered test, not part of the claim: free_names beats free_nonames, paired sign test p < 0.05; it tells whether the names in memory, beyond the ontology's conventions, are what makes the names of a question meet those of the memory; if D2 fails while D1 and D3 pass, the conventions suffice and the finding is reported as such. Not shown whatever the result: questions written by people, open (wh-) questions, negated questions, facts written by people. Expected: free_names within 3 points of canon; free_template near the floor; free_nonames below free_names where a rewording uses a synonym. Estimated cost: gate about $0.6, measurement about $1.1 | to measure (notebook GrandNexus_v7_8_0-rc_phaseD.ipynb) |
